            <div xml:id="d131">

                <pb facs="0280" n="152" sameAs="frus:frus1928v01/pg152"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.0012Anti-War/264: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Fletcher</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Rome</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-08-20T10:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 20,
                                1928—10 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received August 20—9:12
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>85. My telegram No. 84, August 17, 1 p.m.<anchor n="21" xml:id="d131-f1"/> I have
                    just received a personal communication from the Prime Minister the pertinent
                    portion of which I repeat from translation as follows: <pb facs="0281" n="153"
                        xml:id="pg153"/>
                    <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“In view of the numerous engagements which will keep me occupied during
                            the coming week it will not be possible for Under Secretary Grandi, to
                            absent himself at this moment from the Ministry. I am therefore unable
                            to comply, as I would have wished, with the courteous and gratifying
                            desire expressed to me by Your Excellency. I have, however, charged
                            Count Gaetano Manzoni, Royal Ambassador at Paris, who has for this
                            purpose been given full Royal powers, to sign the Kellogg Pact in the
                            name of Italy. I have today formally advised the French Government of
                            this designation.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Fletcher</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
